      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Simon</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"game-container\">\n    <h1>Pixel Simon</h1>\n    <div class=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <p>Level: <span id=\"level\">0</span></p>\n      <p id=\"message\">Press Start to play</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"pads\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Simon game pads\">\n      <button class=\"pad green\" id=\"pad0\" aria-label=\"Green pad\" disabled></button>\n      <button class=\"pad red\" id=\"pad1\" aria-label=\"Red pad\" disabled></button>\n      <button class=\"pad yellow\" id=\"pad2\" aria-label=\"Yellow pad\" disabled></button>\n      <button class=\"pad blue\" id=\"pad3\" aria-label=\"Blue pad\" disabled></button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"startBtn\" aria-label=\"Start game\">Start</button>\n      <button id=\"restartBtn\" aria-label=\"Restart game\" hidden>Restart</button>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": "Main HTML structure with game container, level display, message area, four pads, and start/restart buttons."
    },
    {
      "path": "style.css",
      "content": ":root {\n  --bg: #1e1e2f;\n  --card: #2a2a40;\n  --text: #f0f0f0;\n  --green: #4caf50;\n  --red: #f44336;\n  --yellow: #ffeb3b;\n  --blue: #2196f3;\n  --focus: #ff9800;\n}\n\n* {\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nbody {\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  align-items: center;\n  padding: 16px;\n}\n\n.game-container {\n  background: var(--card);\n  border-radius: 24px;\n  padding: 24px;\n  max-width: 500px;\n  width: 100%;\n  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 24px;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  font-size: 2rem;\n  text-align: center;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n}\n\n.status {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\n}\n\n.status p {\n  margin: 4px 0;\n}\n\n#message {\n  min-height: 1.5em;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  color: #ffcc80;\n}\n\n.pads {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n  gap: 12px;\n  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 400px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n}\n\n.pad {\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: transform 0.1s, box-shadow 0.1s, filter 0.1s;\n  box-shadow: 0 4px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\n  position: relative;\n  opacity: 0.85;\n}\n\n.pad:disabled {\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n  opacity: 0.6;\n}\n\n.pad:hover:not(:disabled) {\n  filter: brightness(1.2);\n}\n\n.pad:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--focus);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\n.pad:active:not(:disabled),\n.pad.active {\n  transform: scale(0.95);\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\n  filter: brightness(1.6);\n}\n\n.green { background: var(--green); }\n.red { background: var(--red); }\n.yellow { background: var(--yellow); }\n.blue { background: var(--blue); }\n\n.controls {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  font-size: 1.1rem;\n  padding: 12px 28px;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 40px;\n  background: #5c5c8a;\n  color: white;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  transition: background 0.2s, transform 0.1s;\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #7a7ab0;\n}\n\nbutton:focus-visible {\n  outline: 3px solid var(--focus);\n  outline-offset: 2px;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: scale(0.96);\n}\n\nbutton[hidden] {\n  display: none;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  body { padding: 8px; }\n  .game-container { padding: 16px; gap: 16px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }\n  .pads { gap: 8px; }\n}\n",
      "description": "Stylesheet defining theme colors, layout, pad states, and responsive design."
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "const pads = [\n  document.getElementById('pad0'),\n  document.getElementById('pad1'),\n  document.getElementById('pad2'),\n  document.getElementById('pad3')\n];\nconst levelEl = document.getElementById('level');\nconst messageEl = document.getElementById('message');\nconst startBtn = document.getElementById('startBtn');\nconst restartBtn = document.getElementById('restartBtn');\n\nlet sequence = [];\nlet playerIndex = 0;\nlet level = 0;\nlet acceptingInput = false;\nlet gameOver = false;\nlet sequenceTimer = null;\n\nfunction setMessage(text) {\n  messageEl.textContent = text;\n}\n\nfunction updateLevel() {\n  levelEl.textContent = level;\n}\n\nfunction flashPad(index, duration = 400) {\n  const pad = pads[index];\n  pad.classList.add('active');\n  setTimeout(() => pad.classList.remove('active'), duration);\n}\n\nfunction playSequence() {\n  acceptingInput = false;\n  pads.forEach(p => p.disabled = true);\n  setMessage('Watch the sequence...');\n  let i = 0;\n  clearInterval(sequenceTimer);\n  sequenceTimer = setInterval(() => {\n    if (i >= sequence.length) {\n      clearInterval(sequenceTimer);\n      sequenceTimer = null;\n      acceptingInput = true;\n      pads.forEach(p => p.disabled = false);\n      setMessage('Your turn');\n      return;\n    }\n    flashPad(sequence[i], 400);\n    i++;\n  }, 600);\n}\n\nfunction nextRound() {\n  level++;\n  updateLevel();\n  playerIndex = 0;\n  sequence.push(Math.floor(Math.random() * 4));\n  playSequence();\n}\n\nfunction handlePadClick(index) {\n  if (!acceptingInput || gameOver) return;\n  flashPad(index, 200);\n  if (sequence[playerIndex] === index) {\n    playerIndex++;\n    if (playerIndex === sequence.length) {\n      acceptingInput = false;\n      pads.forEach(p => p.disabled = true);\n      setMessage('Good! Next round...');\n      setTimeout(nextRound, 800);\n    }\n  } else {\n    endGame();\n  }\n}\n\nfunction endGame() {\n  gameOver = true;\n  acceptingInput = false;\n  clearInterval(sequenceTimer);\n  sequenceTimer = null;\n  pads.forEach(p => p.disabled = true);\n  setMessage('Game over');\n  startBtn.hidden = true;\n  restartBtn.hidden = false;\n  restartBtn.focus();\n}\n\nfunction startGame() {\n  clearInterval(sequenceTimer);\n  sequenceTimer = null;\n  sequence = [];\n  playerIndex = 0;\n  level = 0;\n  gameOver = false;\n  acceptingInput = false;\n  startBtn.hidden = true;\n  restartBtn.hidden = true;\n  updateLevel();\n  setMessage('Get ready...');\n  setTimeout(nextRound, 500);\n}\n\npads.forEach((pad, i) => {\n  pad.addEventListener('click', () => handlePadClick(i));\n});\n\nstartBtn.addEventListener('click', startGame);\nrestartBtn.addEventListener('click', startGame);\n\n// Keyboard support: 1-4 keys\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (gameOver) return;\n  const keyMap = { '1': 0, '2': 1, '3': 2, '4': 3 };\n  if (keyMap[e.key] !== undefined) {\n    handlePadClick(keyMap[e.key]);\n  }\n});\n",
      "description": "Game logic: sequence generation, flashing, player input handling, level tracking, game over and restart."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Simon\n\nA classic Simon memory game with four colored pads, built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No external dependencies.\n\n## How to Play\n\n1. Click **Start** to begin.\n2. Watch the sequence of flashing pads.\n3. Repeat the sequence by clicking the pads (or pressing keys 1–4).\n4. Each successful round adds one more step to the sequence.\n5. A wrong click ends the game — press **Restart** to try again.\n\nThe current level is shown at the top.\n\n## Controls\n\n- **Mouse/Touch:** Click or tap the colored pads.\n- **Keyboard:** Use Tab to focus pads, then Enter/Space to activate. Alternatively, press keys 1, 2, 3, 4 to trigger pads directly.\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- All pads and buttons have ARIA labels.\n- Focus states are clearly visible.\n- Live region announces status changes.\n\n## Run\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser. Works offline.\n",
      "description": "Documentation with game rules, controls, accessibility notes, and how to run."
    }
  ]
